---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Transtyle — the design system compiler" current="home">
  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Design System Compiler</p>
      <h1>One design system.<br /><span class="grad">Every ecosystem.</span></h1>
      <p class="sub">
        Describe your design system once, as standard W3C design tokens. Transtyle compiles it into
        native, idiomatic themes for <strong>eight ecosystems today</strong> — shadcn/ui, daisyUI,
        Apache&nbsp;ECharts, Bootstrap, Storybook, Radix&nbsp;Themes, PrimeNG, and plain CSS variables.
        Deterministic. Explainable. Zero runtime.
      </p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="btn primary" href="/docs/getting-started/">Get started</a>
        <a class="btn" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a>
      </div>

      <div class="terminal">
        <div class="term-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><em>examples/acme</em></div>
        <pre><code><span class="dim">$</span> npx transtyle build shadcn bootstrap echarts

shadcn     <span class="cov-n">42% native</span> · <span class="cov-d">53% derived</span> · <span class="cov-a">3% approximated</span> · 3% dropped
  ↳ dist/shadcn/globals.transtyle.css
bootstrap  ↳ dist/bootstrap/_variables.transtyle.scss
echarts    ↳ dist/echarts/theme.acme-{'{light,dark}'}.json
           ↳ report.json — provenance for every value

<span class="ok">✔ build complete — rebuilds are byte-identical</span></code></pre>
      </div>

      <p class="strip">
        <span>Deterministic — byte-identical rebuilds</span>
        <span>DTCG-native — no lock-in</span>
        <span>Zero runtime — files out, nothing in</span>
        <span>Agent-ready — JSON in, JSON out</span>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="band" aria-labelledby="h-pipeline">
      <h2 id="h-pipeline">A compiler, not a converter</h2>
      <p class="band-sub">The architecture of Babel and LLVM, applied to design systems: pluggable frontends and backends around one intermediate representation. N sources and M targets cost N+M mappings, not N×M converters.</p>
      <div class="pipeline">
        <div class="pipe-col">
          <h3>You write<span class="pipe-tag">token files · importers</span></h3>
          <div class="chip">DTCG token files</div>
          <div class="chip soon">Figma variables</div>
          <div class="chip soon">Tailwind config</div>
          <p class="pipe-note">One source of truth: your names, your values, plain JSON any token tool can read.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pipe-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
        <div class="pipe-col ir">
          <h3>Transtyle compiles<span class="pipe-tag">one shared representation</span></h3>
          <div class="chip ir-chip">normalize · derive ·<br />validate · explain</div>
          <p class="pipe-note">Your tokens bind once to the <a href="/docs/language/">semantic catalog</a> — a pivot vocabulary of <em>meanings</em>, not names. Gaps are filled by deterministic rules.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pipe-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
        <div class="pipe-col">
          <h3>You ship<span class="pipe-tag">native themes · exporters</span></h3>
          <div class="chip">shadcn/ui</div>
          <div class="chip">daisyUI</div>
          <div class="chip">Apache ECharts</div>
          <div class="chip">Bootstrap</div>
          <div class="chip">Storybook</div>
          <div class="chip">Radix Themes</div>
          <div class="chip">PrimeNG</div>
          <div class="chip">CSS variables</div>
          <p class="pipe-note">Idiomatic files per ecosystem — plus a coverage report saying how faithful each one is.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band alt" aria-labelledby="h-derive">
      <h2 id="h-derive">Author 11 tokens — or every single one.</h2>
      <p class="band-sub">Eleven tokens is the floor, not the ceiling. The derivation engine fills every slot you didn't author — hover states, on-colors, tints, dark-mode wiring, a data-viz palette — with deterministic, versioned rules. But every one of those slots is a real, addressable token: <a href="/docs/language/">the catalog</a> exposes the full role grids, elevation ladder, and scales, so you can pin any value — down to a single dark-mode hover state — and derivation yields to you. Authored always wins; every value knows its origin.</p>
      <div class="duo">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-label">You write <span class="prov authored">authored</span></div>
          <pre><code>{`{ "semantic": { "color": {
  "primary": { "solid": "{option.color.blue.600}" },
  "elevation": { "0": { "surface": "…light + dark…" } },
  "text":    { "base": "…", "muted": "…" },
  "border":  "…"
} } }`}</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-label">You get <span class="prov derived">derived</span></div>
          <pre><code>{`--primary: oklch(0.55 0.18 255);
--primary-foreground: oklch(1 0 0); /* contrast-picked, AA ✓ */
--accent: oklch(0.95 0.017 255);    /* brand-tinted */
--chart-1 … --chart-5               /* hue-rotated palette */
+ every hover/active state, light + dark —
  for all eight targets, from the same tokens`}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="band-foot">Ask the compiler why: <code>npx transtyle explain primary.tint</code> prints the value's full provenance chain.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="band" aria-labelledby="h-showcase">
      <h2 id="h-showcase">Same tokens. Native everywhere.</h2>
      <p class="band-sub">This is the whole product in one picture: one token definition on the left, and what each ecosystem's components look like wearing it. Not screenshots — these previews are styled with the actual compiled Acme values.</p>
      <div class="showcase">
        <div class="card show-src">
          <div class="card-label">tokens/semantic.tokens.json</div>
          <pre><code>{`"primary": { "solid":
    "{option.color.blue.600}" },
"danger":  { "solid":
    "{option.color.red.600}" },
"radius":  { "md": "0.5rem" }`}</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div class="show-targets">
          <figure class="tframe">
            <figcaption>Bootstrap</figcaption>
            <div class="t-ui">
              <span class="bs-btn">Primary</span>
              <span class="bs-btn outline">Secondary</span>
              <span class="bs-alert">Something went wrong.</span>
            </div>
          </figure>
          <figure class="tframe dark">
            <figcaption>shadcn/ui · dark</figcaption>
            <div class="t-ui">
              <span class="sc-btn">Continue</span>
              <span class="sc-btn ghost">Cancel</span>
              <span class="sc-input">Email address</span>
            </div>
          </figure>
          <figure class="tframe">
            <figcaption>daisyUI</figcaption>
            <div class="t-ui">
              <span class="dy-btn">Accept</span>
              <span class="dy-badge">error</span>
              <span class="dy-toggle" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
            </div>
          </figure>
          <figure class="tframe">
            <figcaption>Apache ECharts</figcaption>
            <div class="t-ui chart" role="img" aria-label="Bar chart using the derived categorical palette">
              <i style="--h:78%;--c:#026fd7"></i><i style="--h:52%;--c:#d15c56"></i><i style="--h:64%;--c:#319751"></i><i style="--h:38%;--c:#d4a73e"></i><i style="--h:56%;--c:#975ac0"></i>
            </div>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="band-foot">Every example ships <a href="/docs/examples/">runnable demo projects</a> — the same page built with each target's real components, consuming only the compiled <code>dist/</code>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="band" aria-labelledby="h-language">
      <h2 id="h-language">One meaning, every dialect</h2>
      <p class="band-sub">Frameworks disagree on names, not needs. The catalog slot is the <em>meaning</em>; each exporter speaks its target's dialect natively. Your <code>danger</code>, everywhere:</p>
      <div class="xlate">
        <div class="x-src"><span class="sw" style="--c:oklch(0.55 0.19 25)"></span><code>danger.solid</code></div>
        <div class="x-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
        <ul class="x-out">
          <li><code>--destructive</code><em>shadcn/ui</em></li>
          <li><code>$danger</code><em>Bootstrap Sass</em></li>
          <li><code>--color-error</code><em>daisyUI</em></li>
          <li><code>--danger-9</code><em>Radix Themes</em></li>
          <li><code>danger</code> severity<em>PrimeNG preset</em></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <p class="band-foot">The full pivot vocabulary is one page: <a href="/docs/language/">the Transtyle language</a>. Your own names stay yours — you bind them once, with <a href="/docs/adopt-existing/">one-line aliases</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="band alt" aria-labelledby="h-honest">
      <h2 id="h-honest">Honest about lossiness</h2>
      <p class="band-sub">Translation between ecosystems is lossy. Transtyle doesn't hide it — it measures it. Every build classifies every variable, so trust is a number, not a vibe.</p>
      <div class="coverage">
        <div class="cov-bar">
          <span class="seg native" style="width:42%">native</span><span class="seg derived" style="width:53%">derived</span><span class="seg approx" style="width:5%"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="cov-legend">
          <span><i class="dot native" aria-hidden="true"></i> native — lossless, first-class mapping</span>
          <span><i class="dot derived" aria-hidden="true"></i> derived — synthesized by rules, provenance recorded</span>
          <span><i class="dot approx" aria-hidden="true"></i> approximated — mapped, meaning changed; reason given</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band" aria-labelledby="h-plugins">
      <h2 id="h-plugins">Every exporter is a plugin</h2>
      <p class="band-sub">
        The core knows nothing about Bootstrap. All eight official exporters use the same public plugin
        API — resolve the catalog, emit native files, report coverage honestly. The
        <a href="/docs/exporter-css-variables/">css-variables exporter</a> is the reference
        implementation to copy from; the <a href="/docs/internals/">internals guide</a> documents the contract.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="band alt" aria-labelledby="h-agents">
      <h2 id="h-agents">Built for humans <em>and</em> agents</h2>
      <p class="band-sub">
        Deterministic builds, config-as-data, stable diagnostic codes, and a JSON report per build make
        Transtyle operable by AI agents end-to-end — while the compiler itself stays rule-based and auditable.
        Agents write config; the compiler compiles it.
      </p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="btn" href="/docs/ai-agents/">The agent guide</a>
        <a class="btn" href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band final" aria-labelledby="h-start">
      <h2 id="h-start">Start compiling</h2>
      <p class="band-sub">Not yet on npm — you run it from the repository. Four real examples ship with it, including two independently-designed systems (GOV.UK, Carbon).</p>
      <pre class="start"><code>git clone https://github.com/transtyle/transtyle && cd transtyle
npm install
cd examples/acme && npx transtyle build</code></pre>
      <div class="cta center">
        <a class="btn primary" href="/docs/getting-started/">Getting started guide</a>
        <a class="btn" href="/docs/adopt-existing/">I already have a design system</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <style>
    main { max-width: 68rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 clamp(1rem, 4vw, 2.5rem); }
    .hero { text-align: center; padding: 4.5rem 0 3rem; }
    .eyebrow {
      display: inline-block; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--primary); background: var(--primary-soft); padding: 0.3rem 0.9rem; border-radius: 99px;
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono Variable', monospace;
    }
    h1 { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 4rem); line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -0.035em; font-weight: 800; margin: 1rem 0; }
    .grad { background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--primary), var(--violet)); -webkit-background-clip: text; background-clip: text; color: transparent; }
    .sub { max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto 1.6rem; font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
    .sub strong { color: var(--text); }
    .cta { display: flex; gap: 0.8rem; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .cta.center { margin-top: 1.4rem; }
    .btn {
      display: inline-block; padding: 0.6rem 1.3rem; border-radius: 10px; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.95rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--text);
    }
    .btn:hover { text-decoration: none; border-color: var(--text-muted); }
    .btn.primary { background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--primary), var(--violet)); border: none; color: white; }
    .btn.primary:hover { filter: brightness(1.08); }

    .terminal {
      max-width: 42rem; margin: 2.6rem auto 0; border-radius: 14px; overflow: hidden;
      box-shadow: var(--shadow); border: 1px solid var(--border); text-align: left;
    }
    .term-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; padding: 0.6rem 0.9rem; background: var(--bg-soft); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-soft); }
    .term-bar span { width: 11px; height: 11px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--border); }
    .term-bar em { margin-left: auto; font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: normal; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono Variable', monospace; }
    .terminal pre { margin: 0; padding: 1.1rem 1.3rem; background: var(--terminal-bg); color: var(--terminal-text); font-size: 0.83rem; line-height: 1.7; overflow-x: auto; }
    .dim { opacity: 0.6; }
    .ok { color: oklch(0.75 0.15 150); }
    .cov-n { color: oklch(0.78 0.13 150); }
    .cov-d { color: oklch(0.78 0.12 262); }
    .cov-a { color: oklch(0.82 0.12 82); }

    .strip { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem 1.8rem; justify-content: center; margin-top: 2.4rem; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
    .strip span::before { content: '✓ '; color: var(--ok); }

    .band { padding: 3.5rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-soft); text-align: center; }
    .band h2 { font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem); letter-spacing: -0.025em; margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
    .band-sub { max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto 2rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
    .band-foot { max-width: 46rem; margin: 1.6rem auto 0; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; }

    .pipeline { display: flex; align-items: stretch; justify-content: center; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .pipe-col { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 14px; padding: 1.1rem 1.3rem; min-width: 13rem; box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
    .pipe-col h3 { margin: 0 0 0.7rem; font-size: 0.78rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--text-muted); }
    .pipe-arrow { align-self: center; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 1.4rem; }
    .chip { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 0.35rem 0.7rem; margin: 0.4rem 0; font-size: 0.88rem; font-weight: 500; }
    .chip.soon { color: var(--text-muted); border-style: dashed; }
    .chip.soon::after { content: ' · specced'; font-size: 0.72rem; }
    .pipe-col.ir { background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--primary-soft), transparent); border-color: var(--primary); }
    .ir-chip { border: none; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono Variable', monospace; font-size: 0.82rem; }
    .pipe-note { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0.7rem 0 0; max-width: 13rem; }

    .duo { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(19rem, 1fr)); gap: 1.2rem; text-align: left; }
    .card { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 14px; overflow: hidden; box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
    .card-label { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; padding: 0.55rem 1.1rem; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 650; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--text-muted); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-soft); background: var(--bg-soft); }
    .card pre { margin: 0; padding: 1rem 1.2rem; font-size: 0.8rem; line-height: 1.65; overflow-x: auto; background: none; }

    .pipe-tag { display: block; font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 500; text-transform: none; margin-top: 0.15rem; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono Variable', monospace; }

    /* ---- showcase: one token file → four native-looking previews ---- */
    .showcase { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(16rem, 1.1fr) 2fr; gap: 1.2rem; text-align: left; align-items: start; }
    @media (max-width: 860px) { .showcase { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
    .show-targets { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(13rem, 1fr)); gap: 0.9rem; }
    .tframe { margin: 0; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; background: var(--surface); box-shadow: var(--shadow); overflow: hidden; }
    .tframe figcaption { font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 650; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 0.45rem 0.9rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-soft); background: var(--bg-soft); }
    .tframe .t-ui { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 0.55rem; padding: 0.95rem; min-height: 5.4rem; }
    .tframe.dark { background: oklch(0.15 0.012 255); border-color: oklch(0.3 0.02 255); }
    .tframe.dark figcaption { background: oklch(0.19 0.015 255); border-color: oklch(0.28 0.02 255); color: oklch(0.65 0.015 255); }

    /* Bootstrap: its own 0.375rem radius, solid + outline buttons, danger alert */
    .bs-btn { background: oklch(0.55 0.18 255); color: #fff; border-radius: 0.375rem; padding: 0.32rem 0.8rem; font-size: 0.82rem; font-weight: 500; }
    .bs-btn.outline { background: none; color: oklch(0.55 0.18 255); border: 1px solid oklch(0.55 0.18 255); }
    .bs-alert { flex-basis: 100%; background: oklch(0.95 0.025 25); color: oklch(0.42 0.16 25); border: 1px solid oklch(0.88 0.05 25); border-radius: 0.375rem; padding: 0.35rem 0.7rem; font-size: 0.78rem; }
    /* shadcn: the authored 0.5rem radius, dark scheme, input field */
    .sc-btn { background: oklch(0.65 0.16 255); color: oklch(0.13 0.01 255); border-radius: 0.5rem; padding: 0.32rem 0.85rem; font-size: 0.82rem; font-weight: 600; }
    .sc-btn.ghost { background: transparent; color: oklch(0.93 0.005 255); border: 1px solid oklch(0.32 0.02 255); font-weight: 500; }
    .sc-input { flex-basis: 100%; border: 1px solid oklch(0.32 0.02 255); border-radius: 0.5rem; padding: 0.32rem 0.7rem; font-size: 0.78rem; color: oklch(0.55 0.015 255); }
    /* daisyUI: name translation danger→error, toggle control */
    .dy-btn { background: oklch(0.55 0.18 255); color: #fff; border-radius: 0.5rem; padding: 0.32rem 0.85rem; font-size: 0.82rem; font-weight: 600; }
    .dy-badge { background: oklch(0.55 0.19 25); color: #fff; border-radius: 99px; padding: 0.12rem 0.6rem; font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 600; }
    .dy-toggle { width: 2.5rem; height: 1.35rem; border-radius: 99px; background: oklch(0.55 0.18 255); position: relative; display: inline-block; }
    .dy-toggle i { position: absolute; top: 2px; right: 2px; width: calc(1.35rem - 4px); height: calc(1.35rem - 4px); border-radius: 50%; background: #fff; }
    /* ECharts: bars from the derived categorical palette */
    .t-ui.chart { align-items: flex-end; gap: 0.45rem; height: 5.4rem; padding-bottom: 0.7rem; }
    .t-ui.chart i { flex: 1; height: var(--h); background: var(--c); border-radius: 3px 3px 0 0; }

    .xlate { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 1.4rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .x-src { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.3rem; font-size: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; padding: 0.8rem 1.2rem; background: var(--surface); box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
    .x-arrow { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 1.5rem; }
    .x-out { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.35rem; text-align: left; }
    .x-out li { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.8rem; justify-content: space-between; border: 1px solid var(--border-soft); border-radius: 8px; padding: 0.3rem 0.8rem; background: var(--surface); }
    .x-out em { font-style: normal; font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--text-muted); }

    .coverage { max-width: 44rem; margin: 0 auto; }
    .cov-bar { display: flex; height: 2.4rem; border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 650; color: white; box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
    .seg { display: grid; place-items: center; }
    .seg.native, .dot.native { background: var(--cov-native); }
    .seg.derived, .dot.derived { background: var(--cov-derived); }
    .seg.approx, .dot.approx { background: var(--cov-approx); }
    .cov-legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.4rem 1.6rem; justify-content: center; margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
    .dot { display: inline-block; width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 3px; margin-right: 0.4rem; }

    .band.alt { background: transparent; }
    .band.final .start { max-width: 42rem; margin: 0 auto; text-align: left; background: var(--terminal-bg); color: var(--terminal-text); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.1rem 1.3rem; font-size: 0.85rem; overflow-x: auto; }
  </style>
</Base>
